Cap the suffix to `max_chars` and use an early-exit iterator for the length check:

```rust
pub fn truncate_str(s: &str, max_chars: usize) -> String {
    let mut chars = s.chars();
    let prefix: String = chars.by_ref().take(max_chars).collect();
    if chars.next().is_none() {
        // String fits within max_chars — no need to count everything
        return prefix;
    }
    // String is longer; replace the last 3 chars of prefix with "..."
    let cut = max_chars.saturating_sub(3);
    prefix.chars().take(cut).collect::<String>() + "..."
}
```

